Closes CNA-FINDINGS A3 -- Texture2D allocates a mip chain but never fills one, and says "generate".

WHAT IS WRONG
  Texture2D(device, width, height, mipMap, format) sets levelCount_ = CalculateMipLevels(w, h) and
  writes nothing. SetData writes exactly the level it is given. There is no GenerateMipMaps in the
  class. That is faithful to XNA, where mip levels arrive from the content pipeline -- but a game
  that generates its own textures has no content pipeline, and a chain whose lower levels were
  never written shows it the moment the camera pulls back. A city seen from four hundred metres is
  almost entirely minified.

  The header meanwhile says "True to generate a full mipmap chain", which is the one thing it does
  not do.

WHAT THIS CHANGES
  The doc comment says "allocate", and says what to do instead.

  Texture2D::SetDataWithMipsEXT(data, count, sRGB) sets level 0 and box-filters the rest from it,
  averaging in *linear light* when the texels are sRGB-encoded. That is the reason this belongs in
  the engine rather than in each game: sRGB is concave, so the average of four encoded texels is
  brighter than the encoding of their average, and every level comes out paler than the one above.
  A minified city fades towards white as the camera pulls back -- and it is wrong in a way that
  reads as aerial perspective rather than as a bug. Alpha is averaged linearly and never encoded,
  because it is coverage rather than colour; encoding it hardens every soft edge a level at a time.

  cna-city already does this by hand in Materials.cpp (UploadWithMips) -- about forty lines that
  every consumer generating its own textures writes again, and gets wrong in the same way.

STATE OF THIS PATCH
  Applies cleanly (git apply --check) and both patched translation units compile cleanly with the
  exact flags cna-city builds CNA with. It has NOT been run: cnanext is a shared checkout and had
  another session's uncommitted work in modules/platform at the time, so it was not modified.

HOW TO VERIFY IT, FROM THE PROGRAM THAT FOUND IT
    1. git apply this patch in ../../cnanext
    2. in cna-city, replace the body of UploadWithMips in src/Materials.cpp with a Texture2D
       constructed with mipMap = true followed by SetDataWithMipsEXT(pixels, count, sRGB)
    3. cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
    4. ./build/cna-city --camera orbit --time 11.0 --weather clear --fixed-weather \
                        --screenshot shots/mips.png --frames 400

  The aerial view must be indistinguishable from the one cna-city's own chain produces. If the
  suburbs come out paler, the filter is averaging in the encoded space.

